  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: dc6f926697812614b85702b2e9982a93, type: 3}
  m_Name: PrefabNamingConvention
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::PrefabNamingConvention
  conventionText: '<b><size=16>Unity Prefab Naming Convention</size></b>


    This
    naming convention serves as a practical middle ground between Unity and Unreal
    Engine conventions. The prefixes act as quick visual hints to help team members
    and developers instantly understand what type of prefab they''re working with,
    without needing to open it first.


    <b><size=14>Prefix Guide</size></b>


    <b>P_</b>
    - Standard Prefab

    A basic prefab containing any general game object or component
    setup.


    <b>P_V_</b> - Prefab Variant

    A variant of an existing prefab
    with modified properties or components.


    <b>PA_</b> - Prefab Actor

    A
    prefab representing an interactive game entity or character (borrowed from Unreal''s
    "Actor" concept).


    <b>PAV_</b> - Prefab Actor Variant

    A variant of
    an Actor prefab with customized settings.


    <b>PP_</b> - Prefab Pawn

    A
    prefab for controllable characters or entities (using Unreal''s "Pawn" terminology
    for player-controllable objects).


    <b>PAI_</b> - Prefab AI-Controlled Pawn

    A
    prefab specifically for AI-controlled characters, making it clear this entity
    uses autonomous behavior.


    <b>PUI_</b> - Prefab UI

    A prefab containing
    user interface elements.


    <i>Note: These prefixes are organizational tools
    to improve workflow efficiency. They give you an at-a-glance understanding of
    a prefab''s purpose and contents, saving time during development and collaboration.</i>'
